  resultsList:
  - index: 1
    newsTitle: DANDY DOES IN OLD DUFFER
    newsImg: {fileID: -7110462291215695874, guid: 0fe8bf97810c5394582a4c00799d1efd, type: 3}
    lettersList:
    - "To the loathsome, wretched writer of The Weekly Wag,  \r\n\r\nYou cad!  \r\n\r\nYou
      pauper!  \r\n\r\nYou insolent wretch! \r\n\r\nFirst, you show up at my home-
      unannounced! - to harass and badger my family! \r\n\r\nThen, you accuse me-
      whilst I am in the throes of grief- of murdering my beloved brother! \r\n\r\nThen
      - WORST OF ALL \u2013 you condemn me to a life of manacles and striped jumpsuits! 
      \r\n\r\n Rudeness I can forgive, even incarceration- but to be forced to wear
      a striped jumpsuit?!? You have ruined me, sir! And I shall have my revenge! 
      \r\n\r\n My idiotic warden tells me that I am only permitted to send one letter
      a month. Well, let me tell you this, SIR- you can expect another letter from
      me one month hence, detailing the many ways in which I will make you suffer
      upon my escape!  \r\n\r\nYour Mortal Enemy,   \r\n\r\nMaximillian Hold "
    - "Sir, \r\n\r\nRegarding your latest article... \r\n\r\nIt is a hit! Ne\u2019er
      have we had such a salacious story gracing our front page- a famous socialite
      murders his brother in the dead of night- \u2018tis almost Shakespearean! \r\n\r\nAnd
      let me assure you, good sir, your work is paying dividends! I can safely say
      we can keep the paper in print for at least two months or so from the sales
      of this paper alone. Perhaps longer, should our next issue be equally as engaging!
      \r\n\r\nSource me a new story sir, one equally- nay, even more scandalous than
      the last!  \r\n\r\nHave it on my desk by the end of next week. \r\n\r\nThe
      mood on the streets is bleak. Hunger and disease are rife. The poor houses
      are overflowing. And it is our moral obligation to keep the people entertained
      in these  \r\n\r\nThe Weekly Wag \r\nEditor-in-Chief "
  - index: 0
    newsTitle: IDIOT JOURNALIST MANGLES MUDER INVESTIGATION
    newsImg: {fileID: 1867977283544996391, guid: bbd9cf611e781ea4f97a762785fc6ddb, type: 3}
    lettersList:
    - "My Dear Fellow, \r\n\r\nA terrible shame you failed to uncover my brother\u2019s
      killer. I am quite sure it would have made for a thrilling read. Alas, it seems
      my brother\u2019s killer was far too cunning for you, my friend- you have been
      thoroughly outdone! \r\n\r\nAs you seem to be struggling to pen a decent story
      of late, I think it is only right to provide you with some most felicitous
      news: Theodosia and I have wed! I felt it only right to step in as protector
      of my dear departed brother\u2019s family.  \r\n\r\nBy mere happenstance, I
      shall also inherit the vast majority of his fortune. Such joyous news! Wouldn\u2019t
      you agree? \r\n\r\nI am quite sure your readers would be thrilled to hear of
      this wonderful turn of events! Perhaps these lighter news articles are more
      suited to your journalistic skills than a murder investigation. \r\n\r\nYours,
      \r\n\r\nSir Maximillian Hold "
    - "Sir, \r\n\r\nRegarding your latest article... \r\n\r\n\u2018Tis a disaster!
      An unmitigated DISASTER! \r\n\r\nThe quality of your reporting makes me question
      whether you are even literate! \r\n\r\nConflicting evidence. Missing details.
      Libelous assumptions. It is unpublishable! We would be sued for libel for every
      single word written! Did you even visit the manor? Question the suspects? I
      doubt you spent the best part of five minutes there! \r\n\r\nI am docking your
      pay, sir. We have hardly sold a single paper this week as a result of your
      incompetence, and that money is better put towards keeping our printing press
      running. \r\n\r\nGo and source me a new story, sir. This is your last chance,
      and quite possible our paper\u2019s last chance. \r\n\r\nHave it on my desk
      by the end of next week. \r\n\r\nThe Weekly Wag \r\nEditor-in-Chief "
  - index: 2
    newsTitle: KILLER STABLE HAND HANGS!
    newsImg: {fileID: 7497023141891618822, guid: 69a0d2ccda4f3154a99b6fc25d1a9172, type: 3}
    lettersList:
    - "To my dear friend at the Weekly Wag, \r\n\r\nI simply had to inform you- your
      most recent article is the talk of the town! \u201CThe Stable Hand Slasher\u201D
      - A slightly gauche title for my tastes, but a thrilling recount of the events
      all the same! \r\n\r\nYou have my deepest thanks for uncovering that dastardly
      Lavender\u2019s fiendish plot to strike down my poor brother. While Charles
      may have perished, I am sure he rests easy knowing that justice has been carried
      out, and that his beloved brother now cares for his family in his stead. \r\n\r\nIn
      a most pleasing turn of events, I have also recently inherited a sizable portion
      of my dear brother\u2019s estate. As a result, I have made a small donation
      to that wonderful weekly publication of yours as thanks for your thorough investigative
      work. \r\n\r\nShould you have need on me in the future, my feather-quilled
      friend, merely call on me! Maximillian takes care of those who take care of
      him! \r\n\r\nYour biggest fan, \r\n\r\nMaximillian Hold "
    - "Sir, \r\n\r\nRegarding your latest article... \r\n\r\nIt is a hit! Ne\u2019er
      have we had such a salacious story gracing our front page- a famous socialite
      murders his brother in the dead of night- \u2018tis almost Shakespearean! \r\n\r\nAnd
      let me assure you, good sir, your work is paying dividends! I can safely say
      we can keep the paper in print for at least two months or so from the sales
      of this paper alone. Perhaps longer, should our next issue be equally as engaging!
      \r\n\r\nSource me a new story sir, one equally- nay, even more scandalous than
      the last!  \r\n\r\nHave it on my desk by the end of next week. \r\n\r\nThe
      mood on the streets is bleak. Hunger and disease are rife. The poor houses
      are overflowing. And it is our moral obligation to keep the people entertained
      in these difficult times. \r\n\r\nThe Weekly Wag \r\n\r\nEditor-in-Chief "
  sideCaseResultsList:
  - index: 0
    newsTitle: SLOW NEWS DAY
    letter: "Dear Sir, \r\n\r\nLady Theodosia Hold wishes to express her gratitude
      for the manner in which you carried out your investigation at Wenchwatch Hall,
      and for the discretion shown in your article. \r\n\r\nYour exclusion of the
      more salacious details surrounding Admiral Hold\u2019s passing \u2013 whether
      intended or not \u2013 did not go unnoticed. For this, and for the overall
      preservation of her reputation, Lady Hold is most appreciative. She would like
      me to assure you that she will remain an avid consumer of your publication
      for the foreseeable future.  \r\n\r\nWith thanks, \r\n\r\nDorothy Tendwell "
  - index: 1
    newsTitle: AND THEY WERE ROOMMATES
    letter: "Dear Sir, \r\n\r\nI would like to thank you for penning your most recent
      article. \r\n\r\nSeveral months ago, my daughter Dorothy went missing. \r\n\r\nDorothy
      has aways been a sensitive girl and has oft suffered from fits of hysteria
      and anxiety. We believe she fled the family estate during one such episode.
      \r\n\r\nMy wife and I were relieved and appalled in equal measure to discover
      that she was safe and well- working as a housekeeper, no less- and that she
      had fallen under the influence of a deviant stable hand. \r\n\r\nThanks to
      your article, sir, we have been reunited with our daughter, who is now receiving
      proper care. \r\n\r\n Our family physician believes Dorothy\u2019s unnatural
      sexual desires, much like her hysteria, are symptomatic of a greater disease
      at work. Upon his advice, we have had our daughter committed to Bethlem Royal
      Hospital in the hopes a cure can be found for whatever disease plagues her
      mind. \r\n\r\nWe know not yet whether her condition is curable. Curable or
      not, we are thankful that she is now safe, both from the perverse desires of
      that stable hand, and from her own mind. \r\n\r\nWith eternal gratitude, \r\n\r\nJacob
      Tendwell "
  - index: 2
    newsTitle: TWO BROTHERS ONE LOVER
    letter: "Sir, \r\n\r\nI hope you took immense pleasure in sullying my good name,
      for I can think of no other reason barring such a perverse sadism that you
      would have written your most recent article, \u201CTwo Brothers, One Lover.\u201D
      \r\n\r\nYour recent publication has framed me as a woman of loose morals. Worse
      still, you have made me- it pains me to even write the word- unfashionable!
      A social pariah! My social calendar has been thoroughly cleared. Invitations
      have been rescinded! Once constant companions have now all but vanished! \r\n\r\nEven
      Lady Pembroke- who I can assure you has all the grace and class of an Irishman
      in a tavern brawl- has chosen to exclude me from her gala Tuesday week. One
      cannot stress quite how truly low a blow this constitutes. \r\n\r\nOne can
      only hope that The Great Unwashed hastily forget this scurrilous article of
      yours. I, of course, shall never forget what you have done to me. \r\n\r\nYours,
      \r\n\r\nThe Dowager Theodosia Hold "
